        "summary":  "Task-aware knowledge compression (TAKC) is an architectural pattern that compresses entire knowledge bases into task-specific representations rather than relying on similarity-based retrieval as in traditional RAG. The approach surfaces cross-document connections that keyword or embedding search misses and achieves up to 98.4% input token reduction compared to full-context processing. AWS provides a serverless reference implementation using Amazon Bedrock, ElastiCache, and Lambda.",
